							</div>

						</div>

						<div class="memory-item">

							<div class="memory-symbol">
								tan
							</div>

							<div class="memory-arrow">
								↔
							</div>

							<div class="memory-symbol">
								cot
							</div>

						</div>

					</div>

					<div class="remember-card">

						<div class="remember-icon">
							!
						</div>

						<div>

							<span>
								REMEMBER
							</span>

							<strong>
								Reciprocal means 1 divided by the original ratio.
							</strong>

						</div>

					</div>

					<!-- =========================
					     07 · PRACTICE PROBLEMS
					========================= -->

					<div class="topic-label second-label">
						07 · PRACTICE PROBLEMS
					</div>

					<h2>
						Test Your Understanding
					</h2>

					<!-- Example 1 -->
					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">EXAMPLE 1</span>
							<h3>Finding Secant and Product of Tan & Cot</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<p>If cos θ = 5/13, find the value of sec θ and evaluate (tan θ × cot θ).</p>
							<p><strong>Solution:</strong></p>
							<ul>
								<li>sec θ = 1 / cos θ = 1 / (5/13) = <strong>13/5</strong></li>
								<li>Since cot θ is the reciprocal of tan θ, tan θ × cot θ = tan θ × (1 / tan θ) = <strong>1</strong></li>
							</ul>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- Example 2 -->
					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">EXAMPLE 2</span>
							<h3>Evaluating Cosec A + Sec A</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<p>Given tan A = 4/3, evaluate (cosec A + sec A).</p>
							<p><strong>Solution:</strong></p>
							<p>tan A = Perpendicular / Base = 4/3 → Hypotenuse = √(4² + 3²) = 5</p>
							<ul>
								<li>sin A = 4/5 → cosec A = 5/4</li>
								<li>cos A = 3/5 → sec A = 5/3</li>
							</ul>
							<div class="calc-box">
								cosec A + sec A = (5/4) + (5/3)<br/>
								= (15 + 20) / 12 = <strong>35/12</strong>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div class="topic-label second-label">
